I learned that I could
use the word autch-ka

2317
01:27:59,140 --> 01:28:01,140
as an expletive if necessary.

2318
01:28:01,140 --> 01:28:03,140
- Autch-ka.
- Indeed, nice.

2319
01:28:03,140 --> 01:28:04,140
I learned that if you're gonna

2320
01:28:04,140 --> 01:28:06,150
have a general over for dinner,

2321
01:28:06,140 --> 01:28:08,140
you better have turkey
legs and beer on hand.

2322
01:28:08,150 --> 01:28:10,650
(chuckling)

2323
01:28:10,650 --> 01:28:12,650
Well, we learned that
lights and lighting

2324
01:28:12,650 --> 01:28:14,650
aren't really necessary
to make a film these days.

2325
01:28:14,650 --> 01:28:16,660
And neither are actors.

2326
01:28:17,150 --> 01:28:18,650
True, true.

2327
01:28:18,660 --> 01:28:21,160
Well, I think I learned that
I shouldn't go to Saturn

2328
01:28:21,160 --> 01:28:23,160
unless I have the
proper protective gear.

2329
01:28:23,160 --> 01:28:25,160
Yep, yep.

2330
01:28:25,660 --> 01:28:27,660
Yep, and right now, I'm learning

2331
01:28:27,660 --> 01:28:30,160
that even though this movie
is about 80 minutes long,

2332
01:28:30,170 --> 01:28:32,170
it feels like Berlin
Alexanderplatz.

2333
01:28:32,170 --> 01:28:33,670
Yep, yep.

2334
01:28:33,670 --> 01:28:34,670
I also learned
that some sheriffs

2335
01:28:34,670 --> 01:28:35,680
aren't married.

2336
01:28:35,670 --> 01:28:36,670
Did you know that?

2337
01:28:36,670 --> 01:28:38,170
- Yeah.
- I didn't.

2338
01:28:38,180 --> 01:28:40,680
I learned it was impossible
to look good in the 70s.

2339
01:28:42,180 --> 01:28:45,180
I learned that even if you
chop a monster's arm off,

2340
01:28:45,180 --> 01:28:47,690
it'll only make him
stronger and more powerful.

2341
01:28:47,680 --> 01:28:49,180
Yep, and I
learned that you can

2342
01:28:49,190 --> 01:28:51,190
just fill in crucial
elements of the plot

2343
01:28:51,190 --> 01:28:52,690
wherever it's convenient.

2344
01:28:52,690 --> 01:28:54,190
I did not know that.

2345
01:28:54,190 --> 01:28:56,700
No, did not.

2346
01:28:56,690 --> 01:28:58,190
We've learned that
if you're put in charge

2347
01:28:58,200 --> 01:29:00,200
or an urgent, top-secret
government project,

2348
01:29:00,700 --> 01:29:02,200
it really doesn't matter
if you do anything.

2349
01:29:02,200 --> 01:29:03,700
Yep, yep.

2350
01:29:04,700 --> 01:29:06,710
And we learned that sometimes

2351
01:29:06,700 --> 01:29:08,700
people can abuse
spirit gum and latex.

2352
01:29:08,710 --> 01:29:10,210
Oh, I hear ya.

2353
01:29:10,210 --> 01:29:14,710
(mechanical blips and whirs)

2354
01:29:21,720 --> 01:29:23,120
(Crow chitters nervously)

2355
01:29:23,120 --> 01:29:25,120
Well, Crow, this is it.

2356
01:29:25,120 --> 01:29:27,630
This is the day you find
out if Earth versus Soup,

2357
01:29:28,130 --> 01:29:31,130
the project that has
dominated your life for,

2358
01:29:31,130 --> 01:29:32,630
- Years.
- well, years, really,

2359
01:29:32,630 --> 01:29:33,630
gets green-lighted for release.

2360
01:29:33,630 --> 01:29:35,130
You nervous?

2361
01:29:35,130 --> 01:29:37,140
(Crow groans)

2362
01:29:37,130 --> 01:29:38,630
Hello? Crow?

2363
01:29:38,640 --> 01:29:40,140
(Crow screams abruptly)

2364
01:29:40,140 --> 01:29:42,140
Yeah, just get it.

2365
01:29:42,140 --> 01:29:43,640
Hi, guys, everybody here?

2366
01:29:43,640 --> 01:29:45,140
Good, good news, people.

2367
01:29:45,140 --> 01:29:47,150
Clayton, do you wanna tell them?

2368
01:29:47,140 --> 01:29:48,640
Well, the studio's
real excited

2369
01:29:48,650 --> 01:29:50,150
and your movie's
going to be released.

2370
01:29:50,150 --> 01:29:51,650
Oh, wow.

2371
01:29:51,650 --> 01:29:53,150
- That's excellent.
- Well, when's the premiere?

2372
01:29:53,150 --> 01:29:55,660
(all chatter excitedly)

2373
01:29:55,650 --> 01:29:57,150
As a trailer.

2374
01:29:57,150 --> 01:29:58,150
(Crow vocalized shock)

2375
01:29:58,160 --> 01:30:00,160
My movie's gonna be a trailer?

2376
01:30:00,160 --> 01:30:02,160
Uh-huh, this is very exciting.

2377
01:30:02,160 --> 01:30:03,660
This is good news.

2378
01:30:03,660 --> 01:30:06,170
We thought this would give
the widest possible release.

2379
01:30:06,160 --> 01:30:09,660
And it will help us reign
in that marketing budget.

2380
01:30:09,670 --> 01:30:11,670
Well, we still have
a lot of work to do.

2381
01:30:11,670 --> 01:30:14,170
Oh, and there's on thing
that we want to ask,

2382
01:30:14,170 --> 01:30:16,680
and this is going to be
covered in that $800,

2383
01:30:16,670 --> 01:30:19,170
is could you remove your
name from the credits

2384
01:30:19,180 --> 01:30:20,180
as the film's director?

2385
01:30:20,180 --> 01:30:22,680
Again, this is
good news, guys.

2386
01:30:22,680 --> 01:30:24,180
Uh, just a minute.

2387
01:30:24,180 --> 01:30:26,190
Let me get this straight.

2388
01:30:26,180 --> 01:30:28,180
I come to you with a movie.

2389
01:30:28,190 --> 01:30:31,690
You supposedly get me
$30,000,000 to make it.

2390
01:30:31,690 --> 01:30:35,190
You take $29 and a half
million for yourself.

2391
01:30:35,190 --> 01:30:37,200
I get a lousy $800.

2392
01:30:37,190 --> 01:30:38,690
I don't get any credit.

2393
01:30:38,700 --> 01:30:40,700
And my movie's
released as a trailer?

2394
01:30:40,700 --> 01:30:42,200
(Crow cries out in frustration)

2395
01:30:42,200 --> 01:30:43,700
It's okay, it's okay, buddy.

2396
01:30:43,700 --> 01:30:44,700
Uh-huh, that's right.

2397
01:30:45,200 --> 01:30:46,710
Good, we're all
on the same page.

2398
01:30:46,700 --> 01:30:49,700
Now, I'm going to be at
Sundance on Wednesday.

2399
01:30:49,710 --> 01:30:53,210
I'll be in Paris on Friday,
and then Cannes on Saturday.

2400
01:30:53,210 --> 01:30:54,710
So don't try and
get a hold of me.

2401
01:30:54,710 --> 01:30:56,220
Becca, where are those tickets?

2402
01:30:56,710 --> 01:30:58,210
Becca?

2403
01:30:58,220 --> 01:30:59,220
Mother, I think I can
get my whole head in here.

2404
01:30:59,220 --> 01:31:00,220
That's nice, dear.

2405
01:31:00,220 --> 01:31:01,220
Becca, push the button.

2406
01:31:01,720 --> 01:31:02,720
Becca.

2407
01:31:04,120 --> 01:31:08,630
(sweeping music)

2408
01:32:05,680 --> 01:32:07,180
Let's get the hell outta here.

2409
01:32:07,180 --> 01:32:09,110
(plucky chase music)

